			"Message": "chore(Land): Synchronize Element submodule and restore build context for macOS stability\n\nUpdate the Element submodule to integrate the latest macOS rendering fixes and architectural clarifications, while restoring the `.hermes` session directory containing active debugging procedures and patch handoffs for the Tauri/WKWebView integration.\n\n**Element Submodule Updates**:\n- Integrate critical macOS UI stability patches including `content_protected(true)` for traffic light safe zones, deterministic z-index injection plugins (`InjectPartZIndexCSS`), and comprehensive panic safety wrappers (`catch_unwind`) for native FFI boundaries in `Mountain`.\n- Refactor protocol documentation in `Vine` to reflect the distributed gRPC architecture where `.proto` definitions reside within consuming components.\n- Expand architectural documentation across `Air`, `Echo`, `Mist`, and `Worker` with concrete directory trees and standardized PascalCase references.\n\n**Build Context Restoration**:\n- Recreate the `.hermes` directory containing `fixes/active.md`, `tauri/README.md`, `ui/README.md`, and `workflow/rebuild-procedure.md`.\n- These files document applied fixes for Keyring initialization, WKWebView DCL polling, and panic handling, alongside a verification checklist for the native backend and Output transform pipeline.\n- Provide a clear handoff for unresolved UI issues (File Menu z-index, Traffic Light offset) and the VS Code Dependency update.\n\n**Dependency Update**:\n- Synchronize the `Dependency` submodule to upstream `900a349` (Phase 9 agent host crash recovery).\n- This update introduces runtime mutation for live agent sessions, robust subprocess restart mechanisms, and terminal reliability fixes essential for the `Cocoon` extension host.\n\nThese changes ensure the editor maintains stability during complex agent operations, prevents FFI boundary crashes, and preserves the diagnostic context required for ongoing macOS native integration work.",
			"SHA": "f3c5b87a9dce4bdf0ed80e02ebf4c7e82a3cfb70"
		},
